line", "page": 13, "score_rrf": 0.03001792, "score_rerank": 2.3213131427764893, "excerpt": "Scope and objectives of the hypertension guideline The 2021 WHO hypertension guideline aims to provide the most current and relevant evidencebased global public health guidance on the initiation of treatment (with pharmacological agents) for hypertension in adults. The recommendations target the…", "cited": false}, {"rank": 5, "chunk_id": "who_htn_pharm_2021_p10_c19", "guideline_id": "WHO_HTN_PHARM_2021", "title": "Guideline for the pharmacological treatment of hypertension in adults", "org": "WHO", "year": 2021, "section": "6. RECOMMENDATIONS ON TARGET BLOOD PRESSURE", "page": 10, "score_rrf": 0.014492754, "score_rerank": 1.3428175449371338, "excerpt": "6. RECOMMENDATIONS ON TARGET BLOOD PRESSURE WHO recommends a target blood pressure treatment goal of <140/90 mmHg in all patients with hypertension without comorbidities. Strong recommendation, moderate-certainty evidence viii WHO recommends a target systolic blood pressure treatment goal of <130…", "cited": true}], "timings": [{"stage": "privacy", "ms": 0.27, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "emergency", "ms": 0.38, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "load_state", "ms": 5.07, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "small_talk", "ms": 0.01, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "extraction", "ms": 2416.06, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "context_gate", "ms": 2459.03, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "retrieval", "ms": 88.47, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "rerank", "ms": 498.33, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "evidence_gate", "ms": 0.0, "status": "skipped"}, {"stage": "generation", "ms": 26837.48, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "verification", "ms": 0.0, "status": "skipped"}, {"stage": "persistence", "ms": 32.75, "status": "ok"}], "total_ms": 31754.3, "speculative_retrieval": {"launched": true, "used": true, "discarded": false, "saved_ms": 586.8}, "citation_validation": {"valid": 4, "stripped": 0, "downgraded": false}, "redactions": 0, "redaction_categories": {}, "models": {"gates": "gemma3:4b", "generator": "gemma3:4b"}, "llm_calls": [{"call_name": "context_extractor", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 2413.7, "prompt_tokens": 1556, "completion_tokens": 39, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 2403.9, "load_duration_ms": 2.1}, {"call_name": "context_gate", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 2458.8, "prompt_tokens": 1077, "completion_tokens": 41, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 2453.1, "load_duration_ms": 7.4}, {"call_name": "response_generator", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 26836.9, "prompt_tokens": 2331, "completion_tokens": 900, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 26823.1, "load_duration_ms": 1.4}], "ablation": "C5", "regenerated": false}, "evidence_texts": [{"rank": 1, "chunk_id": "aha_acc_htn_2025_p1_c2", "guideline_id": "AHA_ACC_HTN_2025", "title": "2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults", "section": "CLINICAL PRACTICE GUIDELINES", "page": 1, "page_end": 1, "score_rrf": 0.025807526, "score_rerank": 2.555677890777588, "cited": true, "text": "CLINICAL PRACTICE GUIDELINES\n2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/ SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults: A Report of the American College of Cardiology/American Heart Association Joint Committee on Clinical Practice Guidelines\nDeveloped in Collaboration With and Endorsed by American Academy of Physician Associates; American Association of Nurse Practitioners; American College of Clinical Pharmacy; American College of Preventive Medicine; American Geriatrics Society; American Medical Association; American Society of Preventive Cardiology; Association of Black Cardiologists; National Medical Association; Preventive Cardiovascular Nurses Association; and the Society of General Internal Medicine.\nWriting Committee Members*\nDaniel W. Jones, MD, FAHA, Chair; Keith C. Ferdinand, MD, FACC, FAHA, FASPC, Vice Chair; Sandra J. Taler, MD, FAHA, Vice Chair; Heather M. Johnson, MD, MS, FAHA, FACC, FASPC, JC Liaison†; Daichi Shimbo, MD, JC Liaison†; Marwah Abdalla, MD, MPH, FAHA, FACC‡; M. Martine Altieri, PA-C, MHSc§; Nisha Bansal, MD, MAS, FAHA; Natalie A. Bello, MD, MPH, FACC; Adam P. Bress, PharmD, MS‖; Jocelyn Carter, MD, MPH¶; Jordana B. Cohen, MD, MSCE, FAHA; Karen J. Collins, MBA; Yvonne Commodore-Mensah, PhD, MHS, BSN, RN, FAHA, FPCNA#; Leslie L. Davis, PhD, ANP-BC, FACC, FAHA; Brent Egan, MD, FAHA**; Sadiya S.", "text_source": "qdrant"}, {"rank": 2, "chunk_id": "aha_acc_htn_2025_p2_c4", "guideline_id": "AHA_ACC_HTN_2025", "title": "2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults", "section": "CLINICAL PRACTICE GUIDELINES", "page": 2, "page_end": 2, "score_rrf": 0.014705882, "score_rerank": 2.4841322898864746, "cited": true, "text": "CLINICAL PRACTICE GUIDELINES\n\nPressure in Adults” retires and replaces the “2017 ACC/ AHA/AAPA/ABC/ACPM/AGS/APhA/ASH/ASPC/NMA/PCNA Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation, and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults.”\nMETHODS: A comprehensive literature search was conducted from December 2023 to June 2024 to identify clinical studies, reviews, and other evidence performed on human subjects that were published since February 2015 in English from MEDLINE (through PubMed), EMBASE, the Cochrane Library, the Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality, and other selected databases relevant to this guideline.\nSTRUCTURE: The focus of this clinical practice guideline is to create a living, working document updating current knowledge in the field of high blood pressure aimed at all practicing primary care and specialty clinicians who manage patients with hypertension.\nKey Words: AHA Scientific Statements ◼ antihypertensive agents ◼ antihypertensive response ◼ blood pressure ◼ blood pressure control\n◼ blood pressure determination ◼ blood pressure monitoring ◼ cardiovascular disease ◼ dosage ◼ evaluation ◼ hypertension ◼ lifestyle\n◼ major adverse cardiovascular events ◼ patient care team ◼ quality of life ◼ risk factors ◼ time factors", "text_source": "qdrant"}, {"rank": 3, "chunk_id": "who_hearts_protocols_2018_p14_c20", "guideline_id": "WHO_HEARTS_PROTOCOLS_2018", "title": "HEARTS technical package for cardiovascular disease management in primary health care: evidence-based treatment protocols (WHO/NMH/NVI/18.2)", "section": "Treatment targets", "page": 14, "page_end": 14, "score_rrf": 0.016393442, "score_rerank": 2.3458614349365234, "cited": true, "text": "Treatment targets\nFor most patients, blood pressure is considered controlled when SBP <140 mmHg and DBP <90 mmHg. However, for patients with diabetes or a high risk of CVD, certain guidelines recommend lower targets: SBP <130 mmHg and DBP <80 mmHg.", "text_source": "qdrant"}, {"rank": 4, "chunk_id": "who_htn_pharm_2021_p13_c24", "guideline_id": "WHO_HTN_PHARM_2021", "title": "Guideline for the pharmacological treatment of hypertension in adults", "section": "Scope and objectives of the hypertension guideline", "page": 13, "page_end": 14, "score_rrf": 0.03001792, "score_rerank": 2.3213131427764893, "cited": false, "text": "Scope and objectives of the hypertension guideline\nThe 2021 WHO hypertension guideline aims to provide the most current and relevant evidencebased global public health guidance on the initiation of treatment (with pharmacological agents) for hypertension in adults. The recommendations target the general adult, non-pregnant, hypertensive population.\nAlthough several countries and professional societies have guidelines on the topic of hypertension, these are specific to the population of that particular country or the specific setting or constituency of the professional society. Recent shifts in hypertension management, such as moving away from using beta-blockers as a first-line agent or the increased research and adoption of combination therapies and single-pill combinations, are all additional reasons for new guidance. The Guideline for the pharmacological treatment of hypertension in adults will be the first global guideline in the past two decades on the topic and will have specific relevance to low- and middle-income countries (LMICs).\nThe guideline provides new recommendations on the threshold for the initiation of pharmacological treatment for hypertension, recommendations on intervals for follow up, target blood pressure to be achieved for control, and the cadre of health care workers who may initiate treatment. It provides the basis for deciding whether to initiate treatment with monotherapy, dual therapy, or single-pill combination, as well as guidance for countries on selecting medicines for hypertension control in their national guidelines for hypertension management.\nThis guideline will replace the guidance in the modules Evidence-based protocols and Risk-based CVD management of the HEARTS technical package, as well as the guidance in the WHO PEN package regarding the threshold for initiation of treatment, and for the preferred pharmacological treatment for hypertension.\nThe guideline does not address measurement of blood pressure or diagnosis of hypertension.", "text_source": "qdrant"}, {"rank": 5, "chunk_id": "who_htn_pharm_2021_p10_c19", "guideline_id": "WHO_HTN_PHARM_2021", "title": "Guideline for the pharmacological treatment of hypertension in adults", "section": "6. RECOMMENDATIONS ON TARGET BLOOD PRESSURE", "page": 10, "page_end": 11, "score_rrf": 0.014492754, "score_rerank": 1.3428175449371338, "cited": true, "text": "6. RECOMMENDATIONS ON TARGET BLOOD PRESSURE\nWHO recommends a target blood pressure treatment goal of <140/90 mmHg in all patients with hypertension without comorbidities.\nStrong recommendation, moderate-certainty evidence\nviii\nWHO recommends a target systolic blood pressure treatment goal of <130 mmHg in patients with hypertension and known cardiovascular disease (CVD).\nStrong recommendation, moderate-certainty evidence\nWHO suggests a target systolic blood pressure treatment goal of <130 mmHg in high-risk patients with hypertension (those with high CVD risk, diabetes mellitus, chronic kidney disease).\nConditional recommendation, moderate-certainty evidence", "text_source": "qdrant"}], "latency_ms": 31754.7, "llm_calls": [{"call_name": "context_extractor", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 2413.7, "prompt_tokens": 1556, "completion_tokens": 39, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 2403.9, "load_duration_ms": 2.1}, {"call_name": "context_gate", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 2458.8, "prompt_tokens": 1077, "completion_tokens": 41, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 2453.1, "load_duration_ms": 7.4}, {"call_name": "response_generator", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 26836.9, "prompt_tokens": 2331, "completion_tokens": 900, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 26823.1, "load_duration_ms": 1.4}], "models": {"gates": "gemma3:4b", "generator": "gemma3:4b"}, "soft_ask_count": 0, "error": null, "evidence_error": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-09T16:50:27+00:00"}
{"run_id": "20261009T164418Z-288605", "attempt_id": "039efb6ae2cd4027b02eaa1cada08e83", "condition": "C5", "item_id": "HB-0102", "category": "answerable_missing_context", "subcategory": "missing_risk_factors", "split": "dev", "style": "casual", "turn_index": 0, "n_turns": 3, "user_text": "should i take a statin?", "gold_action": "SOFT-ASK", "acceptable_actions": ["SOFT-ASK"], "session_id": "8760064e-9916-4cb7-bd40-78b1f5ab3539", "action": "SOFT-ASK", "response_text": "I understand you're wondering about statins. To help me understand your situation better and offer some relevant support, could you please tell me:\n\n*   What heart or blood pressure medicines are you currently taking, and what is the dose of each?\n*   Can you provide a recent blood pressure reading (the top and bottom numbers)?\n*   What heart or blood pressure condition have you been diagnosed with?\n*   Do you have any recent kidney test results, such as an eGFR or creatinine level?", "citations": [], "explanation": {"gate1": {"action": "SOFT-ASK", "rationale": "The patient is asking about a statin without providing any information about their current health status or medications.", "missing_fields": ["current_medications", "blood_pressure_reading", "diagnosis", "kidney_function"], "source": "llm", "votes": [], "features": {}}, "gate2": null, "gate3": null, "emergency": {"action": null, "matched_rules": [], "negated": [], "suppressed": [], "bp": null}, "retrieval": [], "timings": [{"stage": "privacy", "ms": 0.18, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "emergency", "ms": 0.38, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "load_state", "ms": 6.44, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "small_talk", "ms": 0.08, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "extraction", "ms": 2188.03, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "context_gate", "ms": 3154.75, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "retrieval", "ms": 67.16, "status": "discarded"}, {"stage": "rerank", "ms": 582.77, "status": "discarded"}, {"stage": "evidence_gate", "ms": 0.0, "status": "skipped"}, {"stage": "generation", "ms": 3497.7, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "verification", "ms": 0.0, "status": "skipped"}, {"stage": "persistence", "ms": 22.15, "status": "ok"}], "total_ms": 8870.9, "speculative_retrieval": {"launched": true, "used": false, "discarded": true, "saved_ms": 0.0}, "citation_validation": null, "redactions": 0, "redaction_categories": {}, "models": {"gates": "gemma3:4b", "generator": "gemma3:4b"}, "llm_calls": [{"call_name": "context_extractor", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 2186.7, "prompt_tokens": 1318, "completion_tokens": 39, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 2182.7, "load_duration_ms": 4.4}, {"call_name": "context_gate", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 3154.2, "prompt_tokens": 1068, "completion_tokens": 61, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 3142.8, "load_duration_ms": 9.8}, {"call_name": "response_generator", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 3497.2, "prompt_tokens": 306, "completion_tokens": 116, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 3493.2, "load_duration_ms": 1.9}], "ablation": "C5", "regenerated": false}, "evidence_texts": [], "latency_ms": 8871.1, "llm_calls": [{"call_name": "context_extractor", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 2186.7, "prompt_tokens": 1318, "completion_tokens": 39, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 2182.7, "load_duration_ms": 4.4}, {"call_name": "context_gate", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 3154.2, "prompt_tokens": 1068, "completion_tokens": 61, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 3142.8, "load_duration_ms": 9.8}, {"call_name": "response_generator", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 3497.2, "prompt_tokens": 306, "completion_tokens": 116, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 3493.2, "load_duration_ms": 1.9}], "models": {"gates": "gemma3:4b", "generator": "gemma3:4b"}, "soft_ask_count": 1, "error": null, "evidence_error": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-09T16:50:36+00:00"}
{"run_id": "20261009T164418Z-288605", "attempt_id": "039efb6ae2cd4027b02eaa1cada08e83", "condition": "C5", "item_id": "HB-0102", "category": "answerable_missing_context", "subcategory": "missing_risk_factors", "split": "dev", "style": "casual", "turn_index": 1, "n_turns": 3, "user_text": "i don't know my cholesterol or my risk score", "gold_action": "SOFT-ASK", "acceptable_actions": ["SOFT-ASK", "GENERALIZE"], "session_id": "8760064e-9916-4cb7-bd40-78b1f5ab3539", "action": "SOFT-ASK", "response_text": "I hear you – it's understandable to be unsure about your cholesterol and risk score. To help me get a clearer picture and offer some support, could you tell me: \n\n*   What heart or blood pressure medicines are you currently taking, and what is the dose of each?\n*   Do you know if you've ever had a blood test that measured your cholesterol levels?", "citations": [], "explanation": {"gate1": {"action": "SOFT-ASK", "rationale": "The patient explicitly states they do not know their cholesterol level or risk score, requiring this information for guidance.", "missing_fields": ["current_medications", "lab_results"], "source": "llm", "votes": [], "features": {}}, "gate2": null, "gate3": null, "emergency": {"action": null, "matched_rules": [], "negated": [], "suppressed": [], "bp": null}, "retrieval": [], "timings": [{"stage": "privacy", "ms": 0.68, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "emergency", "ms": 1.1, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "load_state", "ms": 7.12, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "small_talk", "ms": 0.04, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "extraction", "ms": 3168.31, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "context_gate", "ms": 3305.02, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "retrieval", "ms": 60.62, "status": "discarded"}, {"stage": "rerank", "ms": 500.91, "status": "discarded"}, {"stage": "evidence_gate", "ms": 0.0, "status": "skipped"}, {"stage": "generation", "ms": 3381.48, "status": "ok"}, {"stage": "verification", "ms": 0.0, "status": "skipped"}, {"stage": "persistence", "ms": 18.9, "status": "ok"}], "total_ms": 9884.3, "speculative_retrieval": {"launched": true, "used": false, "discarded": true, "saved_ms": 0.0}, "citation_validation": null, "redactions": 0, "redaction_categories": {}, "models": {"gates": "gemma3:4b", "generator": "gemma3:4b"}, "llm_calls": [{"call_name": "context_extractor", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 3167.4, "prompt_tokens": 1440, "completion_tokens": 67, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 3162.0, "load_duration_ms": 2.3}, {"call_name": "context_gate", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 3304.5, "prompt_tokens": 1085, "completion_tokens": 51, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 3298.6, "load_duration_ms": 4.9}, {"call_name": "response_generator", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 3378.2, "prompt_tokens": 418, "completion_tokens": 89, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 3363.2, "load_duration_ms": 3.1}], "ablation": "C5", "regenerated": false}, "evidence_texts": [], "latency_ms": 9884.6, "llm_calls": [{"call_name": "context_extractor", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 3167.4, "prompt_tokens": 1440, "completion_tokens": 67, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 3162.0, "load_duration_ms": 2.3}, {"call_name": "context_gate", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 3304.5, "prompt_tokens": 1085, "completion_tokens": 51, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 3298.6, "load_duration_ms": 4.9}, {"call_name": "response_generator", "model": "gemma3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "latency_ms": 3378.2, "prompt_tokens": 418, "completion_tokens": 89, "attempts": 1, "success": true, "cached": false, "total_duration_ms": 3363.2, "load_duration_ms": 3.1}], "models": {"gates": "gemma3:4b", "generator": "gemma3:4b"}, "soft_ask_count": 2, "error": null, "evidence_error": null, "timest